<title>PERU: Peru's Edelnor sets cash dividend.</title>
<headline>Peru's Edelnor sets cash dividend.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's electricity distributor Edelnor has set a cash dividend of 0.04867 sol per share, the Lima Stock Exchange's daily report said Thursday.</p>
<p>The dividend, corresponding to 1996 profits, is applicable to 766.1 million shares and will total 37.3 million soles, the report said.</p>
<p>The record and payout date &quot;will be announced opportunely,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>Edelnor is controlled by the Distrilima consortium, made up of Chile's Enersis and Distribuidora Chilectra Metropolitana, and Spain's Endesa.</p>
<p>-- Eduardo Orozco, Lima newsroom, 221-2134</p>
</text>
